  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1010 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThe ridge will temporaily flatten on Wednesday as a dry front \nripples across the Mid South/Ohio Valley, bringing some cloud cover \nto the area. However, given the very limited moisture, no \nprecipitation is forecast and some limited heating will still push \nhighs into the 70s. No air mass modification will occur behind the \nfront (save for a reinforcing shot of drier air). In fact, a gradual \nwarming trend will take place late next week as an upper ridge axis \ncentered over the northern Gulf amplifies northward into the \nTennessee Valley and winds veer to the SE/SSE. Highs will climb into\nthe upper 70s on Thursday and the lower 80s in most locations Friday\nand Saturday to close out the month.",
